    "display_name": "Basketball Points",
    "long_instructions": "You’re a sports researcher exploring a dataset used to predict how many points adults can score in basketball based on their height. You want to make sure that your dataset is representative of people of different heights.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. Print the heights of all players who are shorter than 60 inches tall.\r\n2. Print the heights of all players who are at least 60 inches tall but shorter than 70 inches tall.\r\n3. Print the heights of all players who are at least 70 inches tall.\r\n4. Decide whether you think the dataset is representative or not. You’ll answer questions about this dataset in the next level.\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nYou can use an `if` statement inside of a `for` loop to decide whether a piece of code should run for a particular item in the list.\r\n\r\nTo check for multiple conditions in an if statement, use `and` or `or`.\r\n\r\n```python\r\nif condition1 and condition2:\r\n  # This code will only run if both condition1 and condition2 are true\r\n```",
